The '''Stash''' is a reserved "item limbo" where all items go if the player does not have enough inventory space to pick them up.

== Mechanics ==
Items that cannot fit in the player's inventory are automatically placed into either the '''Item''' or '''Material''' Stash depending on the type of the item.
* The '''Item Stash''' holds up to {{Green|720}} non-stackable items, or {{Green|84}} in the [[Rift Dimension]]. Items that bypass this limit are deleted instead of being added to the Stash.
* The '''Material Stash''' can hold an infinite<ref group="note">This count has been documented to reach hundreds of millions, especially in the context of {{Skillname|Mining}}. If an upper limit does exists, it remains unknown as of '''0.25.0.25'''.</ref> amount of stackable items.
If there are items in either Stash, messages will be sent in chat every minute to inform the player. Items can be taken out of their Stash by using the <code>[[Commands|/pickupstash]]</code> command or by pressing the chat message button. The player can also view the contents of either Stash by using the <code>[[Commands|/viewstash]]</code> command (except in the Rift Dimension), or clear all of it by using the <code>[[Commands|/clearstash]]</code> command.

If the player uses <code>[[Commands|/coopsalvage]]</code> to retrieve the items of another player who has left or been kicked from their co-op, the items will go in the Stash if they don't have enough inventory space. This bypasses the normal Item Stash limit.

